@Script library editor
In this editor, you can create script libraries which can then be loaded
in stats in boards. This way, the same script can be used on multiple
boards without needing to make copies of them, and changes will then affect
all of them. Once the script is loaded at run time, the copies will be
independent from each other, so #ZAP etc will only affect the one copy (but
all instances of that stat will be affected).

The .LIB suffix will automatically be added to any lumps you create.

Within scripts in a board (not global scripts or scripts that are loaded at
run time, including other script libraries), if the first line starts with
the two characters @! then the rest is the name of a script library without
the .LIB suffix, and it will be replaced with the specified script library
when the board is loaded at run time.

The other way to load a script library is by the STEX instruction; see the
opcodes.doc file for details. This makes it possible to use script libraries
with dynamic stats and to decide which script library to load at run time.
